# Environment (998 MB). Rebuild with scripts/restore_external.sh
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Third-party author repos (121 MB). Re-clone with scripts/restore_external.sh.
# Kept out deliberately: other people's repositories, reference-only per CLAUDE.md #2.
reference/

# Model checkpoints and embeddings. Large and regenerable from kernels/ + run_gate1.py.
# Summaries, histories and logs ARE tracked.
*.npz

# 251 MB of paper PDFs. The extracted full texts are tracked as .txt instead.
related papers/papers/
*.pdf

# arXiv HTML dumps; the extracted .txt is what we actually read.
*.html
!related papers/graphify-out/graph.html

# Graphify cache
related papers/graphify-out/cache/

# Rendered panels (90 MB and growing: 67 runs x ~5 PNGs). Derived data, regenerated by
# `PYTHONPATH=. .venv/bin/python scripts/render_all.py` from the .npz artifacts -- which
# are themselves gitignored, so tracking the pictures but not their sources was backwards.
# figures/INDEX.md IS tracked: it is the readable numeric record.
figures/**/*.png
figures/**/*.pdf
!figures/INDEX.md

# Scratch
nohup.out

# Per-run stdout from scripts/run_n7_all.sh. Same reason as the launcher logs below:
# untracked files make provenance.git_dirty() true, which would stamp every artifact of
# an 18-hour run as "not reproducible from the recorded SHA alone".
logs/

# Launcher process logs. Transient and regenerable -- the lab record is LAB_NOTEBOOK.md.
# They must be ignored or they dirty the tree and taint the git SHA baked into a kernel.
*launch.log
*chain.log
# Analysis stdout captures: regenerable, and tracking one dirties the tree at the
# exact moment the next run stamps its provenance.
results/**/*.txt
results/*.txt

# Overleaf bundle: retired 2026-09-28 (local LaTeX); kept ignored so a stale copy never lands.
paper/overleaf_bundle.zip
# ...and the same bundle unzipped in place. paper/check_tex.py skips it by name; anything
# else that copies the sources under paper/ is a FAILURE there, not a silent doubling.
paper/overleaf_bundle/
build/

# TMLR submission build outputs (scripts/build_tmlr.sh); OPENREVIEW.md is tracked.
TMLR/*.zip
TMLR/abstract.txt

# arXiv build outputs (scripts/build_arxiv.sh); abstract.txt and SUBMIT.md are tracked.
for arxiv/*.tar.gz
for arxiv/main.pdf
# Zenodo upload (4.8 GB, the deposit itself); SUBMIT.md and description.txt are tracked.
for zenodo/*.tar.zst
